## Requirements

[uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) is the only tool you need. It installs Python {{ python_version }}+
and every development tool on demand, on Windows, macOS, and Linux.

## Getting started

```bash
uv sync                      # create .venv and install the project with its dev group
uv lock                      # create uv.lock, then commit it for reproducible installs
uv run {{ package_name }} --help
uv run {{ package_name }} hello --name World
```

## Development

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Run tests with coverage | `uv run pytest` |
| Lint | `uv run ruff check .` |
| Format | `uv run ruff format .` |
| Type-check | `uv run mypy {{ package_name }}` |
| Build sdist and wheel | `uv build` |
| Install git hooks | `uvx pre-commit install` |

Add runtime dependencies with `uv add <package>` and development tools with
`uv add --dev <package>`.

{% if 'mcp' in components -%}
## MCP server

`{{ package_name }}/mcp_server.py` exposes the package to AI agents as
[Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) tools over stdio.

```bash
uv run {{ project_name }}-mcp          # serve; an MCP client starts this for you
```

`.mcp.json` registers the server for agents that work in this repository, such as Claude Code.
To use it from another client, give that client the same command and arguments. Add a tool by
decorating a typed function with `@server.tool()`.

